<!--
  The icon, compiled into the binary.

  The platform's own icon (the Windows resource, the macOS bundle) is what
  Explorer, the Dock and the taskbar draw, and it covers the cases where
  the operating system never asks the process. This one covers the cases
  where it does: the X11 window icon, the Wayland fallback when no
  .desktop file has been installed, and anywhere the app draws its own
  identity.

  Compiled in rather than loaded from a path, because a path that is
  correct in the build tree, in an AppImage and inside a .app is three
  different paths, and the failure is a silently missing icon.

  Two sizes, not five: Qt scales between the ones it is given, and these
  are the two ends of the range a window icon is asked for.
-->
<RCC>
  <qresource prefix="/">
    <file alias="sstvae-48.png">icons/sstvae-48.png</file>
    <file alias="sstvae-256.png">icons/sstvae-256.png</file>
  </qresource>
</RCC>
